lib/ukpod: include <uk/assert.h>

anon.c calls UK_ASSERT but includes only its own header, so the assertion
compiles as an implicit function call and the link fails:

    lib/ukpod/anon.c:23: undefined reference to `UK_ASSERT'

Unavoidable for any virtio-fs build: LIBUKFS_VIRTIOFS needs the posix-vfs
stack, which pulls in ukfs-ramfs, which selects LIBUKPOD_ANON.

Found against unikraft 0.21.0 (Ijiraq).
--- a/lib/ukpod/anon.c
+++ b/lib/ukpod/anon.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 /* Page I/O ops for anonymous memory */
 
+#include <uk/assert.h>
 #include <uk/pod/anon.h>
 
 /**
